<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Local XSS Lab</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/levels.css">
</head>
<body>
  <main class="wrap">
    <header><p class="eyebrow">LOCAL TRAINING ENVIRONMENT</p><h1>XSS Vulnerability Lab</h1>
      <p>Practice all three XSS topics at easy, medium, and hard difficulty.</p></header>
    <div class="notice"><strong>Safety boundary:</strong> this lab binds to 127.0.0.1. Use harmless proof-of-execution payloads and never test systems without permission.</div>
    <section class="cards">
      <article class="difficulty-card"><h2>Reflected XSS</h2><p>Trace request data into different HTML and JavaScript contexts.</p><ul class="level-links">
        <li><a class="level-link easy" href="/reflected?level=easy">Easy — HTML body</a></li>
        <li><a class="level-link medium" href="/reflected?level=medium">Medium — HTML attribute</a></li>
        <li><a class="level-link hard" href="/reflected?level=hard">Hard — JavaScript string</a></li>
      </ul></article>
      <article class="difficulty-card"><h2>Stored XSS</h2><p>Follow saved comments as they are rendered in progressively more complex contexts.</p><ul class="level-links">
        <li><a class="level-link easy" href="/stored?level=easy">Easy — HTML body</a></li>
        <li><a class="level-link medium" href="/stored?level=medium">Medium — HTML attribute</a></li>
        <li><a class="level-link hard" href="/stored?level=hard">Hard — JavaScript string</a></li>
      </ul></article>
      <article class="difficulty-card"><h2>DOM-based XSS</h2><p>Trace browser-controlled URL data into client-side HTML sinks.</p><ul class="level-links">
        <li><a class="level-link easy" href="/dom?level=easy">Easy — fragment to HTML</a></li>
        <li><a class="level-link medium" href="/dom?level=medium">Medium — fragment to attribute</a></li>
        <li><a class="level-link hard" href="/dom?level=hard">Hard — query to HTML after decoding</a></li>
      </ul></article>
    </section>
    <h2>Hunter workflow</h2>
    <ol><li>Identify input sources: query strings, forms, URL fragments.</li><li>Trace where input goes: HTML, attributes, JavaScript, or DOM sinks.</li><li>Test only with harmless proof-of-execution payloads.</li><li>Record impact, reproduction steps, and a remediation.</li></ol>
  </main>
</body></html>